    {
        "name": "Pre-ovulatory Follicular Stasis",
        "name_ja": "排卵前卵胞停滞",
        "symptoms": {"abdominal_swelling", "anorexia", "lethargy", "weight_loss"},
        "description": "Pre-ovulatory Follicular Stasis is a reproductive condition where ovarian follicles fail to undergo ovulation, leading to chronic egg retention.",
        "description_ja": "カメレオンやフトアゴヒゲトカゲに多い卵巣卵胞が排卵されない状態です。",
        "urgency": "high",
        "recommended_tests": ["ultrasound", "radiographs", "blood_chemistry"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Hormonal imbalance: inadequate GnRH signaling from hypothalamus, ovarian dysfunction, lack of luteinizing hormone surge; 2) Environmental: inadequate photoperiod (<10-12h depending on species), improper temperature cycling, lack of male presence/breeding stimulus; 3) Nutritional: calcium deficiency, vitamin A deficiency, poor body condition; 4) Systemic disease: obesity, liver disease, renal dysfunction, chronic illness.",
        "causes_ja": "トカゲにおける排卵前卵胞停滞の原因：ホルモン異常（視床下部GnRH不足、卵巣機能不全、LH分泌低下）。環境：光周期不足（<10-12時間、種による）、温度サイクル不適切、雄の不在/交配刺激不足。栄養：カルシウム欠乏、ビタミンA欠乏、不良な体況。全身疾患：肥満、肝疾患、腎機能不全、慢性疾患。",
        "pathophysiology": "Pre-ovulatory follicular stasis represents a failure of the hypothalamic-pituitary-ovarian (HPO) axis to generate the cyclic GnRH/LH surge necessary for follicle rupture and ovulation. Follicles remain sequestered within ovarian tissue, progressively accumulate yolk (lipid), increasing in size. Follicle atresia may occur (follicular degeneration) or follicles persist indefinitely. Large follicles compress adjacent tissues, causing abdominal distension. Chronic yolk absorption from atretic follicles may lead to peritonitis or coelomitis. Calcium sequestration within maturing follicles precipitates hypocalcemia if severe/chronic.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "排卵前卵胞停滞は視床下部-下垂体-卵巣軸（HPO軸）が卵胞破裂/排卵に必要な周期的GnRH/LH分泌を生じない病態。卵胞は卵巣組織内に残留し進行性に卵黄（脂質）が蓄積→サイズ増大。卵胞自家溶解（atresia）が生じるか、卵胞が無期限に停滞。大型卵胞は隣接組織を圧迫→腹部膨満。慢性的な自家溶解卵胞の卵黄吸収で腹膜炎/体腔炎。重度/慢性例では卵胞内カルシウムシークエスター化で低カルシウム血症。",
        "treatment": "Environmental management: Increase photoperiod to 12-14h/day (species-dependent, e.g., bearded dragons prefer 14h summer photoperiod), establish temperature cycling (3-5°C day/night differential), ensure proper nesting substrate availability. Medical intervention: GnRH agonist leuprolide 0.05-0.1 mg/kg IM or hCG 500-1000 IU/kg IM to stimulate ovulation (if follicles viable). Supportive care: IV fluids (50-100 mL/kg/day) if dehydration, analgesia (meloxicam 0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h), calcium gluconate 50-100 mg/kg IV/IC (if hypocalcemia present), vitamin A supplementation 4,000-10,000 IU/kg, vitamin E 50-200 IU/kg. Surgical: Ovariohysterectomy if follicles are atretic/non-responsive to medical management, persistent coelomitis, or recurrent stasis. Post-treatment: Long-term environmental optimization, weight management, species-appropriate breeding season simulation.",
        "treatment_ja": "トカゲにおける排卵前卵胞停滞の治療：環境管理：光周期延長（12-14時間/日、種による。フトアゴは夏場14時間推奨）、温度サイクル確立（日中/夜間3-5℃差）、産卵床材確保。医学的介入：GnRHアゴニスト（リュープロレリン0.05-0.1 mg/kg IM）またはhCG 500-1000 IU/kg IM で排卵刺激（卵胞が生存している場合）。支持療法：輸液（脱水時 50-100 mL/kg/日）、鎮痛（メロキシカム0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h）、低カルシウム血症時にグルコン酸カルシウム 50-100 mg/kg IV/IC、ビタミンA補充 4,000-10,000 IU/kg、ビタミンE 50-200 IU/kg。外科：卵胞が自家溶解/医学的管理無反応、持続的な体腔炎、再発性停滞時に卵巣卵管摘出。術後：長期環境最適化、体重管理、種別繁殖季節シミュレーション。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: proper photoperiod (12-14h/day depending on species, e.g., bearded dragons 14h summer), temperature cycling (3-5°C differential day/night), appropriate nesting environment with suitable substrate, balanced calcium-rich diet (Ca:P 1.5-2:1), regular body weight monitoring, avoidance of obesity, seasonal breeding rest periods, and regular veterinary examinations. For captive lizards, environmental enrichment and species-appropriate social/sexual stimulation may reduce stasis incidence.",
        "prevention_ja": "排卵前卵胞停滞の予防：適切な光周期（12-14時間/日、種による。フトアゴは夏場14時間）、温度サイクル（日中/夜間3-5℃差）、適切な産卵環境と基質、バランスカルシウム食（Ca:P 1.5-2:1）、定期的な体重監視、肥満回避、季節的繁殖休止期、定期獣医診察。種別の環境エンリッチメント・交配刺激でstasis発症率低減。",
        "prognosis": "Prognosis good to excellent with early environmental correction and medical management. Ovariohysterectomy results in permanent resolution but precludes future breeding. If environmental factors are corrected and follicles are viable, ovulation-induction therapy (GnRH agonist, hCG) succeeds in 60-75% of cases. Chronic/severe stasis with atretic follicles and coelomitis carries poorer prognosis.",
        "prognosis_ja": "排卵前卵胞停滞の予後：早期の環境改善と医学的管理で予後良好。卵巣卵管摘出で永続的解決だが繁殖不可。環境是正と卵胞生存時、排卵誘発療法（GnRHアゴニスト、hCG）で60-75%成功。慢性/重度stasis with atretic follicles・体腔炎では予後慎重。",
        "onset_pattern": {"subacute", "chronic"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young", "adult", "senior"},
    },
    {
        "name": "Cloacal Prolapse",
        "name_ja": "総排泄腔脱",
        "symptoms": {"tissue_prolapse", "cloacal_swelling", "straining", "anorexia", "lethargy"},
        "description": "Cloacal Prolapse involves protrusion of colon, oviduct, or urinary bladder through the cloaca, often secondary to straining.",
        "description_ja": "結腸、卵管、膀胱が関与する可能性のある総排泄腔組織の突出です。",
        "urgency": "emergency",
        "recommended_tests": ["physical_exam", "radiographs", "ultrasound"],
        "causes": "Caused by: 1) Excessive straining: constipation (impaction, dystocia, egg binding), diarrhea, parasitic infection (endoparasites), tenesmus; 2) Metabolic: hypocalcemia (calcium-dependent smooth muscle dysfunction), dehydration, malnutrition; 3) Anatomical: cloacal structure abnormalities, rectal/colonic weakness; 4) Systemic disease: chronic inflammatory bowel disease, neoplasia affecting GI tract.",
        "causes_ja": "トカゲの総排泄腔脱の原因：過度なストレイニング（便秘/下痢、難産、卵詰まり、内寄生虫感染、しぶり）。代謝性：低カルシウム血症（カルシウム依存性平滑筋機能不全）、脱水、栄養不良。解剖学的：総排泄腔構造異常、直腸/結腸筋力低下。全身疾患：慢性炎症性腸疾患、GI腫瘍。",
        "pathophysiology": "Cloacal prolapse results from excessive straining or pressure against a weakened cloacal wall (from hypocalcemia or anatomical factors). As straining increases intra-luminal pressure, the mucosa is forced through the cloacal opening. Prolapsed tissue becomes edematous from venous/lymphatic obstruction. Prolonged exposure to air/trauma causes mucosal drying, necrosis, and bacterial colonization. Tissue necrosis (dark purple/black discoloration) indicates irreversibility and necessitates resection. Large prolapses can impair fecal/urate passage and cause secondary impaction.",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "総排泄腔脱はストレイニング亢進または低カルシウム血症/解剖学的弱点による総排泄腔壁脆弱化で生じる。内腔圧亢進で粘膜が総排泄腔開口から押し出される。脱出組織は静脈/リンパ閉塞で浮腫→空気暴露/外傷で粘膜乾燥・壊死・細菌コロニー化。組織壊死（暗紫色/黒変）は不可逆性→切除必要。大型脱出は糞便/尿酸塩通過障害→二次性便秘。",
        "treatment": "Emergency management: 1) Tissue viability assessment: Viable tissue is pink/red with normal bleeding; necrotic tissue is dark purple/black and desiccated. 2) Edema reduction: Apply hypertonic (50%) dextrose solution or honey (10-15 min) to reduce swelling before reduction. 3) Gentle reduction: Under sedation (propofol 5 mg/kg IV or alfaxalone 5 mg/kg IV) or light general anesthesia (isoflurane), gently manipulate prolapsed tissue back through cloaca using blunt instrument and lubricant. 4) Prevention of re-prolapse: Place 3-0 or 4-0 absorbable suture as purse-string around cloacal rim (leave space for fecal/urate passage). Suture remains 2-3 weeks. 5) Treat underlying cause: Address constipation (fluids, dietary fiber, stool softener docusate 2-5 mg/kg), egg binding (see Egg Binding protocol), parasitism (antiparasitic therapy). 6) Antibiotics if contamination: enrofloxacin 5-10 mg/kg IM/IV q48h × 14 days. 7) Post-reduction: Rest (limit activity), pain management (meloxicam 0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h × 7 days), nutritional support, monitor for re-prolapse or straining.",
        "treatment_ja": "総排泄腔脱の緊急管理：1) 組織生存性評価：生存組織は淡紅色～赤で出血正常；壊死組織は暗紫色～黒で乾燥。2) 浮腫軽減：50%高張ブドウ糖液またはハチミツ（10-15分）を塗布して浮腫軽減。3) 温和な還納：鎮静（プロポフォール5 mg/kg IV またはアルファキサロン5 mg/kg IV）下または軽い全身麻酔（イソフルラン）下で、脱出組織を鈍的器具と潤滑剤で総排泄腔に優しく還納。4) 再脱出予防：3-0または4-0吸収性糸で総排泄腔周囲をパースストリング縫合（糞便/尿酸塩通過スペース確保）。糸は2-3週間保持。5) 根本原因治療：便秘対策（輸液、食物繊維、スツール軟化剤docusate 2-5 mg/kg）、卵詰まり治療（卵詰まりプロトコル参照）、寄生虫症治療。6) 汚染時の抗菌薬：エンロフロキサシン5-10 mg/kg IM/IV q48h × 14日。7) 還納後：安静（活動制限）、鎮痛（メロキシカム0.1-0.2 mg/kg IM q48h × 7日）、栄養補給、再脱出/ストレイニング監視。",
        "prevention": "Prevention includes: appropriate husbandry with species-specific dietary fiber content, adequate hydration (misting/water bowl access), parasite control (regular fecal exams, antiparasitic treatment if needed), balanced calcium diet (Ca:P 1.5-2:1), proper temperature (species POTZ), avoidance of chronic constipation-promoting conditions, and prompt treatment of diarrheal/GI diseases.",
        "prevention_ja": "総排泄腔脱の予防：種特異的食物繊維含有食、十分な給水（ミスティング/飲料ボウル）、寄生虫制御（定期糞便検査、必要時駆虫）、バランスカルシウム食（Ca:P 1.5-2:1）、種別至適温度、慢性便秘促進条件回避、下痢/GI疾患の迅速治療。",
        "prognosis": "Good for viable tissue when reduced promptly (within 24-48h). Recurrence: ~30% with purse-string suture alone (recurrence at 2-3 weeks post-suture removal). Colopexy (suturing colon to body wall internally) may be needed for recurrent prolapses. Necrotic tissue requires surgical resection (prognosis depends on extent). Early intervention and treatment of underlying cause improves outcomes.",
        "prognosis_ja": "生存組織で迅速還納時（発症から24-48時間以内）予後良好。再発率：パースストリング単独で～30%（縫合抜去後2-3週で再発）。再発性脱出にはcolopexy（大腸を体壁に内部固定）必要。壊死組織は外科的切除必要（予後は切除範囲による）。早期治療と根本原因治療で予後改善。",
        "onset_pattern": {"acute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"young", "adult", "senior"},
    },
